    {
      "name": "search_account_collaborators",
      "title": "Search Account Collaborators",
      "summary": "Lists SITE collaborators across your Pressable account — people on at least one of your sites — with pagination and filters. Use this instead of list_account_collaborators for large accounts to avoid oversized responses. Filter by email, email_domain, name, role, site_id, or state. Page through results with page and per_page (max 200). Set unique: true to collapse to one row per person (with a site_count) instead of one row per collaborator-site pairing. Someone with only account-level access and no site collaboration will not appear — use get_collaborator_access or list_new_site_default_collaborators for account-level-only access. Returns total_collaborators, page, per_page, and the collaborators for the page.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "list_unique_collaborators",
      "title": "List Unique Collaborators",
      "summary": "Lists each SITE collaborator on your Pressable account once (deduplicated across sites), with a site_count and whether they have account-level access. A SITE collaborator is someone on at least one of your sites; unlike list_account_collaborators (one row per collaborator-site pairing), this stays small even when a person is on many sites — use it to inventory who collaborates on your sites. Filter by email, email_domain, name, role, or state; page with page and per_page (max 200). Someone with only account-level access and no site collaboration will not appear — use get_collaborator_access or list_new_site_default_collaborators for account-level-only access.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "get_collaborator_access",
      "title": "Get Collaborator Access",
      "summary": "Reads a collaborator's account-level access — their new-site default permissions: whether they are an Account Administrator (account_administrator), are auto-added to new sites (add_to_all_new), can create sites, manage tags, manage Single Sign-On (manage_sso), see the Usage page (view_usage), manage billing (manage_billing), manage business email (manage_email), their notification settings, and the default site roles applied to new sites (new_site_roles). These top-level flags are the stored grants. They are not a complete update_collaborator_access input: delegate_email_notification_capabilities is not reported here, and the update takes the new_site_roles as roles. effective_capabilities is a read-only map of the same keys showing what the collaborator can actually do: an Account Administrator reports every capability it implies true there (except delegate_email_notification_capabilities, which this read does not report). The read counterpart to update_collaborator_access. Provide the collaborator's email.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "list_new_site_default_collaborators",
      "title": "List New Site Default Collaborators",
      "summary": "Lists every collaborator your account automatically adds to new sites, with the site roles applied on add — your account's \"new site\" collaborator policy. Use get_collaborator_access for one person's full account-level settings.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "get_account_collaborator_summary",
      "title": "Get Account Collaborator Summary",
      "summary": "Summarizes one collaborator on your account: their account-level access (new-site default permissions), how many of your sites they collaborate on (site_count), and the distribution of site roles they hold across those sites. account_access carries the stored capability flags (account_administrator, view_usage, manage_billing, manage_email, create_site and the rest) plus a read-only effective_capabilities map of the same keys showing what the collaborator can actually do (an Account Administrator holds every capability it implies, except delegate_email_notification_capabilities, which this read does not report). Provide the collaborator's email. Use search_account_collaborator_sites to page through the specific sites.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "search_account_collaborator_sites",
      "title": "Search Account Collaborator Sites",
      "summary": "Lists the sites a specific collaborator is on within your account, with pagination — use this instead of get_account_collaborator_sites when the collaborator is on many sites. Provide the collaborator's email; page through with page and per_page (max 200). Returns each site's id, name, state, roles, and WordPress username.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "count_account_collaborators",
      "title": "Count Account Collaborators",
      "summary": "Returns the number of collaborators on your account matching the given filters — a cheap way to size the result before calling search_account_collaborators or list_unique_collaborators. Counts SITE collaborators only (people on at least one of your sites); someone with only account-level access and no site collaboration is not counted — use get_collaborator_access or list_new_site_default_collaborators for account-level-only access. Filter by email, email_domain, name, role, site_id, or state. Set unique: true to count distinct people instead of collaborator-site pairings.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "add_site_collaborators",
      "title": "Add Site Collaborators",
      "summary": "Adds multiple collaborators to a Pressable site in one call — instead of calling add_site_collaborator once per person. Provide site_id and a collaborators array of { email, roles }. Roles you supply for a person are applied as-is; if you omit a person's roles and use_account_defaults is true (the default), their account-level new-site default roles are applied — so you can add a team to a transferred site as if it were new without looking up each person's roles. Requires MANAGE_COLLABORATORS on the site. Returns a per-collaborator result (added or failed) so partial failures are visible. Idempotent: re-adding an existing collaborator updates their roles. Call get_collaborator_roles for valid role names; list_new_site_default_collaborators to see who has new-site defaults.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "grant_collaborator_role",
      "title": "Grant Collaborator Role",
      "summary": "Grants a single site role to one or more collaborators who are already on a site, WITHOUT changing their other roles — the safe way to make a permission tweak (e.g. give several people manage_dns). Unlike add_site_collaborator and add_site_collaborators, which replace a person's entire role set, this only adds the one role. Provide site_id, role, and emails. To add someone who is not yet on the site, use add_site_collaborators. Requires MANAGE_COLLABORATORS. Returns a per-collaborator result. Call get_collaborator_roles for valid role names.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "revoke_collaborator_role",
      "title": "Revoke Collaborator Role",
      "summary": "Removes a single site role from one or more collaborators on a site, WITHOUT removing the collaborator or touching their other roles — the safe way to take away one permission (e.g. remove manage_dns from several people). Unlike add_site_collaborator and add_site_collaborators, which replace a person's entire role set, this only removes the one role. Provide site_id, role, and emails. To remove people from the site entirely, use remove_site_collaborators. Requires MANAGE_COLLABORATORS. Returns a per-collaborator result. Call get_collaborator_roles for valid role names.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "remove_site_collaborators",
      "title": "Remove Site Collaborators",
      "summary": "Removes multiple collaborators from a Pressable site in one call — instead of calling remove_site_collaborator once per person. Provide site_id and emails; optionally set delete_wp_user to also delete each person's WordPress user. Only affects people currently on the site. Requires MANAGE_COLLABORATORS. Returns a per-collaborator result (removed or failed) so partial failures are visible. To remove only a specific permission rather than the whole collaborator, use revoke_collaborator_role instead.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "bulk_add_collaborators_to_sites",
      "title": "Bulk Add Collaborators To Sites",
      "summary": "Adds one or more collaborators to MANY sites in a single call — the account-wide version of add_site_collaborators. Provide a collaborators array of { email, roles } and site_ids; use [-1] as site_ids to target every site you can manage. Roles you supply for a person are applied as-is; omit a person's roles and their account-level new-site default roles are used when use_account_defaults is true (the default). The change runs in the background and returns an operation_id immediately — poll get_collaborator_bulk_operation with that id to see per-site, per-collaborator results. Each person is authorized individually, so a person you lack permission over comes back as a failed entry instead of failing the run. Use add_site_collaborators instead when you only need one site. Call get_collaborator_roles for valid role names.",
      "category": "collaborators"
    },
    {
      "name": "bulk_grant_collaborator_role",
